### Model Design & Architectural Evolution
Our final model architecture is the result of an iterative engineering process aimed at balancing baseline capacity with robustness.

1. Iteration 1 (Baseline Pipeline Check)
* Architecture: 2-Block Convolutional Neural Network (CNN).
* Details: 3x3 kernels, Max Pooling, and a single Linear classification head.
* Goal: Establish a working data pipeline, verify the 80/20 train/validation split, and ensure the hardware-agnostic saving mechanism operated correctly.
* Result: Pipeline successfully executed and passed the local evaluation wrapper.

2. Iteration 2 (Scaling Capacity)
* Architecture: 4-Block CNN with Batch Normalization and Global Average Pooling.
* Details: Replaced the brittle hardcoded flattened tensor with AdaptiveAvgPool2d to ensure dimensional stability. Introduced nn.BatchNorm2d after every convolution to stabilize training gradients and nn.Dropout(p=0.5) to act as our initial regularizer.
* Goal: Increase the network's expressive power to achieve high accuracy on clean, in-distribution images.
* Result: [Leave blank until you record your clean accuracy]

